#### Track selection

In this analysis both primary and global tracks are used. In order to identify the charge particles and to ensure the quality of data several track quality cuts are applied to the reconstructed tracks from the TPC detector. Short tracks were eliminated from the analysis by requiring that all tracks have atleast 15 hit fit points in the TPC. The effect of track-splitting by the tracking algorithm is minimized by the number of fit points are more than half the number of total possible hit points for a track. Pile-up tracks are identified during the data production and flagged with an ID greater than 1000. All tracks with the flag between 0 to 1000 are selected for the analysis. To ensure that the tracks comes from the primary vertex, a requirement is placed on the DCA between the track and the event vertex. All tracks within the pseudo-rapidity range of \(|\eta|<1.0\) are selected. A list of the track cuts applied on individual tracks are shown in the Table 3.4.

