### 3.4 Reconstruction of strange and multi-strange hadrons

In this section, we discuss the methods for reconstructing strange and multi-strange hadrons \(K^{0}_{\rm s}\), \(\phi\), \(\Lambda+\bar{\Lambda}\), \(\Xi+\bar{\Xi}\) and \(\Omega+\bar{\Omega}\) at mid-rapidity (\(|y|<\) 1.0) in U+U collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{\rm NN}}\) = 193 GeV. A summary of their properties of decays are listed in the Table 3.5[31].

#### \(\phi\) reconstruction

\(\phi\)-meson is reconstructed using invariant mass technique through it's hadronic decay channel: \(\phi\to K^{+}K^{-}\) (branching ratio = 48.9 \(\pm\) 0.5%) [32]. Decay daughter kaon tracks are identified using both the TPC and TOF detector. Kaon \(m^{2}\) information is used whenever a TOF matched track is available, otherwise TPC \(dE/dx\) information is used to identify kaon tracks. The track selection cuts for the \(\phi\)-meson reconstruction in U+U collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{\rm NN}}\) = 193 GeV is listed in the Table 3.6.

