### 4.6 \(\phi\)-meson \(v_{2}\) extraction

The method for \(\phi\)-meson \(v_{2}\) extraction is discussed in the chapter 3. \(\phi\)-meson \(v_{2}\) measurement in Au+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{\rm NN}}=14.5\) GeV is done using the \(\phi-\psi\) binning method. The raw yield of \(\phi\)-meson, extracted in the previous section is measured in the bins of angle (\(\phi-\psi_{2}\)), where \(\phi\) is the azimuthal angle of \(\phi\)-meson in the lab-frame and \(\psi_{2}\) is the \(2^{nd}\)-order event plane angle. The measured distribution \(dN/d(\phi-\psi_{2})\) is fitted with the functional form of Fourier function to extract \(v_{2}\).

The raw yields extracted as discussed above for \(\phi\)-meson at mid-rapidity for minimum-bias (0-80%) Au+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{\rm NN}}=14.5\) GeV are shown in the Fig. 4.6. The obtained raw yields are fitted with the function,

\[\frac{dN}{d(\phi-\psi_{2})}=A\left(1+2v_{2}^{obs}\cos n(\phi-\psi_{2})\right), \tag{4.9}\]

where \(A\) and \(v_{2}^{obs}\) are the fit parameters. The measured \(v_{2}^{obs}\) values obtained from fit are divided by the appropriate event plane resolution to get final \(v_{2}\) values. The \(p_{T}\) dependence of \(v_{2}\) is studied by repeating the above procedure for fixed ranges in

