Multiplicity weights are

\[w_{\langle 2^{\prime}\rangle}\equiv m_{p}M-m_{q} \tag{4.39}\]

\[w_{\langle 4^{\prime}\rangle}\equiv(m_{p}M-3m_{q})(M-1)(M-2). \tag{4.40}\]

The two and four-particle differential cumulants without detector bias are given by

\[d_{n}\{2\}=\langle\langle 2^{\prime}\rangle\rangle \tag{4.41}\]

\[d_{n}\{4\}=\langle\langle 4^{\prime}\rangle\rangle-2\times\langle\langle 2^{ \prime}\rangle\rangle\langle\langle 2\rangle\rangle. \tag{4.42}\]

