Systematic uncertainties

Systematic uncertainties on \(v_{2}\) are estimated by varying event and track selection parameters e.g. collision vertex position, the DCA of the primary vertex for the tracks, and the number of fit points used for reconstruction of the tracks etc. Table 4.7 lists all the parameters that were varied for the systematic uncertainties together with the default value.

Systematic uncertainties are calculated using method suggested in the Ref. [31]. The statistical effect on systematic uncertainties are taken into account using this method. Systematic uncertainties are calculated as follows:

1. First, difference between the \(v_{2}\) values obtained from the default cut (listed in Table 4.7) and the \(v_{2}\) values from different variations are calculated, which is denoted as: \[\Delta v_{2}=(v_{2})_{i^{th}sys}-(v_{2})_{def}\] (4.45)
2. The quadratic difference between the statistical error on \(v_{2}\) in default case and

