Figure 4.14 (left panel) shows inclusive charged hadron \(v_{2}\) as a function of \(p_{T}\) for various collision centrality classes in Au+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{\rm NN}}=14.5\) GeV. The results are obtained using \(\eta\)-sub event plane method at mid-rapidity (\(|\eta|<1.0\)). The \(v_{2}(p_{T})\) shows monotonic increasing trend with increasing \(p_{T}\) for Au+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{\rm NN}}=14.5\) GeV. The right panel of Fig. 4.14 presents the \(p_{T}\)-intigrated \(v_{2}\) as a function of \(\eta\) for various centrality classes. The \(v_{2}(\eta)\) has a weak dependence on \(\eta\). Also, there is a clear centrality dependence observed for both \(v_{2}(p_{T})\) and \(v_{2}(\eta)\). These dependence is similar to other beam energies for BES [11].

#### 4.9.3.2 \(v_{2}\) methods comparison: non-flow effects

